Parameter Setting: Set the currently used objective lens to 40×; Set the filter set to DAPI fluorescence mode; 
#Auxiliary Operation: First automatically configure the camera exposure time for DAPI channel, then set the light source brightness to 0, and finally perform automatic focusing on the current field of view.; 
#Image Automatic Acquisition Parameter Setting: Configure the filter set to DAPI fluorescence mode with the current exposure parameter; configure the XY position parameter to the current stage position with size matching the current field of view; do not configure Z-axis stack parameters; do not configure time parameters.; 
#Image Automatic Acquisition: Perform automatic image acquisition using the configured parameters to capture the DAPI channel image.; 
#Parameter Setting: Set the filter set to TRITC fluorescence mode; 
#Auxiliary Operation: Automatically configure the camera exposure time for TRITC channel; set the light source brightness to 0.; 
#Image Automatic Acquisition Parameter Setting: Configure the filter set to TRITC fluorescence mode with the current exposure parameter; configure the XY position parameter to the current stage position (same as DAPI) with size matching the current field of view; do not configure Z-axis stack parameters; do not configure time parameters.; 
#Image Automatic Acquisition: Perform automatic image acquisition using the configured parameters to capture the TRITC channel image.

Initialization: Initialize the cell segmentation model, enable GPU acceleration, and select a segmentation model type suitable for nucleus segmentation.; 
#Image Reading: Read the acquired DAPI channel image data.; 
#Segmentation Inference: Execute cell segmentation inference on the DAPI image to output segmentation masks.; 
#Masks Analysis: Analyze the segmented nucleus masks to calculate and extract the centroid coordinates of each nucleus.; 
#Analysis Saving: Save the extracted centroid coordinates as a JSON file.; 
#Resource Release: Release model resources and clean up the environment.

