#Image Automatic Acquisition Parameter Setting: Configure the filter set to brightfield mode and set the corresponding exposure parameter to a low value suitable for brightfield imaging (e.g., 10ms); configure the XY position parameter to the current stage position with size requirements matching the current field of view; do not configure Z-axis stack parameters; do not configure time parameters; 
#Image Automatic Acquisition: Perform automatic image acquisition using the configured parameters to capture a single plane brightfield image of the iPSC colony

Initialization: Initialize the cell segmentation model, enable GPU acceleration, and select a segmentation model type suitable for identifying individual cells in brightfield images; 
#Image Reading: Read the acquired brightfield image data from the microscope operation platform; 
#Segmentation Inference: Execute cell segmentation inference on the read image to output a dictionary containing segmentation masks, flow fields, and cell feature style vectors; 
#Masks Analysis: Analyze the segmented masks to calculate the total count of detected objects (cells); 
#Analysis Saving: Save the analysis result, specifically the total count of detected objects, as a JSON object; 
#Resource Release: Release model resources and clean up the environment

